<td id="S4.T6.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T6.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T6.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T6.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">51</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T6.2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">101</span></td>
<td id="S4.T6.2.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">190</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The physics method reaches 90% accuracy at epoch 51—a <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.1\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.1\times</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> speedup</span> over baseline (epoch 106) and <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.2\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\times</annotation></semantics></math> over 1cycle (epoch 112). This is consistent with the oscillator model’s prediction that critical damping produces the shortest settling time. Note the plateau cost is visible on this seed too: physics reaches 95% last (epoch 190).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T7" class="ltx_table">
