</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.6 </span>Prediction Verification</h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The three qualitative predictions hold as follows:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fastest early convergence—confirmed.</span> Physics reaches 90% in approximately half the epochs of baseline (multi-seed: <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.34\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.34</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.34\times</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reduced oscillation—partially confirmed.</span> Test accuracy is not strictly monotone for any method at this scale; physics shows smaller epoch-to-epoch oscillation than baseline during epochs 1–60 (mean <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\text{acc}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>acc</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\text{acc}|</annotation></semantics></math> 2.23 vs. 2.57 pp; largest single-epoch drop 5.25 vs. 7.22 pp on seed 42).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Competitive final accuracy—confirmed with a caveat.</span> The single-seed gap looks like noise, but the multi-seed analysis shows a systematic <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.46" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.46</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.46</annotation></semantics></math> pp deficit (<math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.009" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.009</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.009</annotation></semantics></math>), which the hybrid recipe removes (Section <a href="#S9" title="9 Experiment 4: Hybrid Momentum Scheduling ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.7 </span>Damping Regime Analysis</h3>

<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2603.28921v3/fig_regimes.svg" id="S4.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/164;" width="476" height="164"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Damping regime classification across 200 epochs. Red = underdamped (<math id="S4.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&gt;\mu_{c}+0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&gt;\mu_{c}+0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), green = critically damped (<math id="S4.F3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mu-\mu_{c}|\leq 0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mu-\mu_{c}|\leq 0.05</annotation></semantics></math>), blue = overdamped (<math id="S4.F3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu&lt;\mu_{c}-0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu&lt;\mu_{c}-0.05</annotation></semantics></math>). Classification uses the applied (clamped) momentum. The baseline is underdamped for 85% of training; physics is mildly underdamped for the first 66 epochs of the clamped phase (the clamp is active through epoch 84) and critically damped thereafter, never overdamped.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each epoch, we classify the regime by comparing the actual momentum <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> to the critical value <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{c}=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{c}=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, using a tolerance of <math id="S4.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mu-\mu_{c}|\leq 0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mu-\mu_{c}|\leq 0.05</annotation></semantics></math> for the critical band.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Damping regime classification across 200 training epochs.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T8.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<th id="S4.T8.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T8.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Underdamped</span></th>
<th id="S4.T8.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T8.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Critical</span></th>
<th id="S4.T8.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T8.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overdamped</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T8.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T8.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Baseline (<math id="S4.T8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>)</th>
<td id="S4.T8.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">169 (84.5%)</td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">21 (10.5%)</td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">10 (5%)</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T8.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T8.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">1cycle (Smith)</th>
<td id="S4.T8.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">175 (87.5%)</td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">25 (12.5%)</td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">0 (0%)</td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T8.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T8.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T8.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Physics</span></th>
<td id="S4.T8.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T8.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">66 (33%)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T8.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">134 (67%)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T8.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="S4.T8.2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0 (0%)</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">All rows classify the momentum <em id="S4.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">actually applied</em> (i.e., after clamping for physics). The baseline operates in the underdamped regime for <span id="S4.SS7.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">85% of training</span>—the standard configuration (<math id="S4.SS7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>) spends the vast majority of training oscillating rather than converging optimally. Physics is never overdamped and is within the critical band for the final 134 epochs (67%); during the clamped early phase it is mildly underdamped with <math id="S4.SS7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\mu|\leq 0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>0.13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\mu|\leq 0.13</annotation></semantics></math>—four times closer to critical than the baseline’s <math id="S4.SS7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\mu=+0.53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.53</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\mu=+0.53</annotation></semantics></math> at epoch 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Why this matters for diagnostics.</span> The damping regime analysis is not just a training diagnostic—it is the <em id="S4.SS7.p3.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">foundation</em> for the error-localization pipeline in Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Experiment 2: The Diagnostic Pipeline ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. The fact that the baseline is heavily underdamped suggests that its learned representations may be suboptimal in specific layers, which we can now identify and correct.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Generalization Across Architecture and Dataset</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The multi-seed validation (Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiment 1: Multi-Seed Validation of the Schedule ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) establishes the schedule on
ResNet-18/CIFAR-10. Two natural objections remain: the effect could depend on
the skip-connection structure of residual networks, and it could depend on the
dataset. We address both with a matched training protocol (200-epoch cosine
learning-rate schedule <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1\to 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1\to 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch
size 128, three seeds); minor per-experiment implementation differences (cosine
phase convention, dataset normalization constants) are documented in the
released code.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Architecture: VGG-16 Without Skip Connections</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Skip connections are a plausible confounder: they reshape the loss landscape
that the oscillator model damps, so a residual-only validation leaves open
whether the schedule exploits that structure. We train VGG-16(BN) adapted to
CIFAR-10 (global average pooling, single linear head).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>VGG-16(BN)/CIFAR-10, three seeds. Epochs to 90% test accuracy and
best accuracy; speedup is per-seed <math id="S5.T9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ep}_{\text{baseline}}/\text{ep}_{\text{physics}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>ep</mtext><mtext>baseline</mtext></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mtext>ep</mtext><mtext>physics</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ep}_{\text{baseline}}/\text{ep}_{\text{physics}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T9.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Method</th>
<th id="S5.T9.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Best acc (mean<math id="S5.T9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>std)</th>
<th id="S5.T9.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Epochs<math id="S5.T9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>90%</th>
<th id="S5.T9.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Speedup</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T9.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T9.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Baseline (<math id="S5.T9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="94.01\pm 0.28\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>94.01</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.28</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">94.01\pm 0.28\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128.7\pm 8.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>128.7</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>8.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128.7\pm 8.4</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">—</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T9.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T9.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Physics (<math id="S5.T9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="93.64\pm 0.07\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>93.64</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.07</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">93.64\pm 0.07\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="75.7\pm 6.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>75.7</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>6.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">75.7\pm 6.7</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T9.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T9.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.72\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.72</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.72\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The speedup replicates on an architecture with no skip connections
(<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.72\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.72</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.72\times</annotation></semantics></math> to 90% on average; per-seed <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.91/1.80/1.43\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.91</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.80</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>1.43</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.91/1.80/1.43\times</annotation></semantics></math>, 3/3 seeds,
paired <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=6.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=6.15</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{df}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>df</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{df}=2</annotation></semantics></math>, two-sided <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.026" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.026</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.026</annotation></semantics></math>), and the early-training
advantage is larger still (up to <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="4.9\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>4.9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4.9\times</annotation></semantics></math> to 85% on individual seeds). The
best-accuracy deficit of the pure physics schedule also replicates (<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.07" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.07</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.07</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S5.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.61" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.61</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.61</annotation></semantics></math> pp), consistent with the ResNet-18 result: the fast-early/slow-top
profile is a property of the schedule, not of the architecture. We did not run
a hybrid arm on VGG; given that both the speedup and the deficit replicate, we
expect the Hybrid-90 recipe (Section <a href="#S9" title="9 Experiment 4: Hybrid Momentum Scheduling ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) to transfer, but this
remains to be validated directly.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Dataset: CIFAR-100</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On CIFAR-100, ResNet-18 does not reach 90% top-1 accuracy, so we define the
milestone relative to the baseline: the first epoch at which a method reaches
95% of the baseline’s final best accuracy. Absolute threshold curves are
reported alongside in the released data.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>ResNet-18/CIFAR-100, three seeds. Milestone = epochs to reach 95% of
the baseline’s final best top-1 accuracy.</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T10.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T10.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T10.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Method</th>
<th id="S5.T10.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Best acc (mean<math id="S5.T10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math>std)</th>
<th id="S5.T10.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Epochs<math id="S5.T10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math>milestone</th>
<th id="S5.T10.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Speedup</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T10.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Baseline (<math id="S5.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78.77\pm 0.33\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>78.77</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.33</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78.77\pm 0.33\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="152.7\pm 1.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>152.7</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>1.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">152.7\pm 1.2</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">—</td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T10.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T10.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Physics (<math id="S5.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="77.07\pm 0.06\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>77.07</mn><mo>±</mo><mrow><mn>0.06</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">77.07\pm 0.06\%</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="134.3\pm 3.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>134.3</mn><mo>±</mo><mn>3.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">134.3\pm 3.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S5.T10.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T10.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.14\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.14</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.14\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">On CIFAR-100 the effect is smaller: the early-training speedup persists
(reaching 60% top-1 accuracy <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.9\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.9\times</annotation></semantics></math> faster and 65%
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.3</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3.9\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3.9</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3.9\times</annotation></semantics></math> faster than the baseline), but the pure schedule pays a
larger final-accuracy cost (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1.70" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.70</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1.70</annotation></semantics></math> pp on average, 3/3 seeds), which compresses
the accuracy-matched milestone gain to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.14\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.14</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.14\times</annotation></semantics></math> (0/3 seeds above
<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.3\times</annotation></semantics></math>). The milestone is threshold-sensitive in the direction one would
expect from the deficit: at 97% of the baseline’s best accuracy the pure
schedule is no faster (<math id="S5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="0.99\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.99</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.99\times</annotation></semantics></math> mean), and at <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="98\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>98</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">98\%</annotation></semantics></math> it fails to reach the milestone on two of three seeds and is
slower than the baseline on the third — at the top end, the accuracy cost
dominates the early speed. We therefore scope the speedup claim to the settings where it is
demonstrated — CIFAR-10 across two architecture families — and report the
CIFAR-100 result as a boundary of applicability. We note that this boundary
<em id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strengthens</em> the case for the hybrid recipe: the harder the dataset, the
more of the schedule’s value lies in its early phase, which is exactly the
phase the hybrid keeps. Validating Hybrid-90 on CIFAR-100 is future work.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Experiment 2: The Diagnostic Pipeline</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section describes the surgical-correction protocol and the original (version 2) experiment. <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reader note (v3):</span> the layer-<em id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">selection</em> interpretation of this experiment is refuted by the exhaustive baseline of Section <a href="#S8" title="8 Experiment 3b: The Exhaustive Layer-Selection Baseline ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>—the selected triple performs no better than a random 3-of-7 pick. The protocol itself, its reproducibility, and the attribution ranking remain valid and are prerequisites for Section <a href="#S8" title="8 Experiment 3b: The Exhaustive Layer-Selection Baseline ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Hypotheses</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">H1: Error-specific gradient attribution localizes problem layers.</span> On misclassified test images, gradient norms should concentrate in specific layers rather than being uniformly distributed, producing a sparse layer-level diagnostic. <em id="S6.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Note:</em> gradient attribution is a well-established technique; what is new here is computing it <em id="S6.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exclusively on misclassified images</em> to identify “sick” layers rather than generally important ones.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">H2: Targeted correction is more efficient than full retraining.</span> Retraining only the identified problem layers should fix errors with <math id="S6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math>80% compute savings.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">H3: Different damping trajectories produce different errors.</span> Models trained with different momentum schedules should make qualitatively different errors.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Step 1 — Scan: Cross-Model Error Analysis</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute per-image predictions for all three models on the 10,000-image CIFAR-10 test set:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Cross-model error analysis on CIFAR-10 test set.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T11.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T11.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T11.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T11.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Category</span></th>
<th id="S6.T11.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T11.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Count</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T11.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T11.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Common errors (all 3 methods wrong)</td>
<td id="S6.T11.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">215</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T11.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T11.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Only baseline wrong</td>
<td id="S6.T11.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right">104</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T11.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T11.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Only physics wrong</td>
<td id="S6.T11.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right">138</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T11.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T11.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Only 1cycle wrong</td>
<td id="S6.T11.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right">96</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T11.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T11.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Physics correct, baseline wrong</td>
<td id="S6.T11.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb">172</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The 172 images correctly classified by the physics model but not by the baseline provide direct evidence that optimization trajectory affects learned representations (H3 confirmed). These are not random differences: they cluster around specific feature confusions, as shown below.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Step 2 — Localize: Gradient Attribution on Misclassified Images</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute per-layer gradient norms on the baseline model’s 452 misclassified test images. Critically, we restrict the computation to <em id="S6.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">errors only</em>—this asks “which layers are most confused on the specific images the model gets wrong?” rather than “which layers are generally most important?”</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span>Per-layer gradient norms on misclassified images (baseline model). Layers above the median are flagged as problem layers.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T12.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T12.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T12.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T12.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer</span></th>
<th id="S6.T12.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T12.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Function</span></th>
<th id="S6.T12.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T12.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grad Norm</span></th>
<th id="S6.T12.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T12.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Status</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T12.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T12.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Mid-level features (shapes, parts)</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T12.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10.56</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Problem</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T12.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Low-level features (textures, edges)</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S6.T12.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9.14</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Problem</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T12.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Early-mid features (patterns)</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S6.T12.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8.58</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Problem</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T12.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Very early features</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">7.43</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Normal</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T12.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer4</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">High-level features</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">7.38</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Normal</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T12.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Batch normalization</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4.99</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Normal</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T12.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T12.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S6.T12.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fc</span></td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Final classifier</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.86</td>
<td id="S6.T12.2.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Normal</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result (H1 confirmed).</span> Gradient norms concentrate in three layers (<span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span>, <span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span>, <span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span>), with a <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="12.3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>12.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12.3\times</annotation></semantics></math> ratio between the highest (<span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span>: 10.56) and lowest (<span id="S6.SS3.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fc</span>: 0.86) layers, and a <math id="S6.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="1.15\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.15</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.15\times</annotation></semantics></math> ratio between the third-highest problem layer and the fourth-highest normal layer. The distribution is sparse, not uniform—the pipeline produces a clear cut between “sick” and “healthy” layers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4 </span>Step 3 — Diagnose: Error Taxonomy</h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The most frequent confusion pairs cluster around texture–shape confusions in the problem layers:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Most frequent confusion pairs in the baseline model with layer attribution.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T13.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S6.T13.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T13.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T13.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">True</span></th>
<th id="S6.T13.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T13.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Predicted</span></th>
<th id="S6.T13.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T13.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attributed Layer</span></th>
<th id="S6.T13.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T13.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Root Cause</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T13.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">cat</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">dog</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S6.T13.2.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Face shape, furry texture</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">dog</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">cat</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T13.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Reverse confusion</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">cat</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bird</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T13.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Compact silhouette</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">deer</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">dog</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T13.2.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Brown texture <math id="S6.T13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> “dog”</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">horse</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bird</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T13.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Green background dominates</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">ship</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">airplane</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S6.T13.2.7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Horizontal shape</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T13.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S6.T13.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">frog</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">dog</td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S6.T13.2.8.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span></td>
<td id="S6.T13.2.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Color confusion</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each error has a <em id="S6.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">causal explanation</em>: <span id="S6.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span> confuses based on texture (brown <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> dog, green <math id="S6.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> bird); <span id="S6.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span> confuses based on shape (compact silhouette, horizontal shape); <span id="S6.SS4.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span> confuses based on mid-level features (face shape, fur, color). The diagnostic pipeline does not just identify <em id="S6.SS4.p2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">that</em> errors exist—it explains <em id="S6.SS4.p2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">why</em> each error occurs and <em id="S6.SS4.p2.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">which layer</em> is responsible.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.5 </span>Step 4 — Treat: Surgical Correction</h3>

<div id="S6.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Protocol.</span> We freeze all 120 parameter tensors in the baseline model, then unfreeze only the three problem layers (<span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span>, <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span>, <span id="S6.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer2</span>; 35 tensors). We retrain for 30 epochs with physics momentum at <math id="S6.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\max}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\max}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math> (10<math id="S6.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> lower than original training).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span>Surgical correction results: retrain 3 of 7 layer groups for 30 epochs with physics momentum.</figcaption>
<table id="S6.T14.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S6.T14.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T14.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metric</span></th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T14.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Before</span></td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="S6.T14.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">After</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Accuracy</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">95.48%</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">95.54%</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Total errors</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">452</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">446</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Errors fixed</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">55</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">New errors</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">49</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Net improvement</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">+6</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Compute (epochs <math id="S6.T14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> layers)</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">30 <math id="S6.T14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 3 layers</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">vs. full retraining</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">200 <math id="S6.T14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> all layers</td></tr>
<tr id="S6.T14.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S6.T14.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Compute savings (epoch-wise)</th>
<td id="S6.T14.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">—</td>
<td id="S6.T14.2.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">85%</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Result (H2 confirmed).</span> Surgical correction fixed 55 errors by retraining only 29% of parameters (35/120 tensors) for 15% of the original training duration—an 85% epoch-wise compute saving versus full retraining, on 29% of the parameters. The net improvement (+6) in this initial experiment is modest; a stronger variant is tested in Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Experiment 3: Cross-Optimizer Invariance and Diagnostic Comparison ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.6 </span>Step 5 — Verify: Analysis of Side Effects</h3>

<div id="S6.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The 49 new errors after correction are expected: retraining at the layer-group level affects many parameters simultaneously, and some previously correct features are perturbed. This can be mitigated through: (1) per-residual-block correction instead of per-layer-group, (2) elastic weight consolidation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to preserve correct features, and (3) iterative diagnose–correct–verify cycles. Section <a href="#S7" title="7 Experiment 3: Cross-Optimizer Invariance and Diagnostic Comparison ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> shows that choosing layers more carefully (via iKFAD-guided selection) achieves the best net result (+22; 62 fixed, 40 new errors).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Experiment 3: Cross-Optimizer Invariance and Diagnostic Comparison</h2>

<div id="S7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment tests the most important question for scaling: <em id="S7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">does the diagnostic generalize across optimizers?</em> If gradient attribution on misclassified images identifies the same problem layers regardless of how the model was trained, then the pipeline can be applied to any model—including LLMs trained with Adam variants.</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train five models under identical conditions (ResNet-18, CIFAR-10, 200 epochs, cosine LR, seed 42):</p>
<ol id="S7.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline</span>: SGD + constant <math id="S7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Physics (ours)</span>: SGD + <math id="S7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(t)=1-2\sqrt{\alpha(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(t)=1-2\sqrt{\alpha(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">iKFAD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>: per-parameter adaptive friction <math id="S7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> tracking kinetic energy.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>: cubically damped SGD (<math id="S7.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=0.1</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S7.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adam</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>: <math id="S7.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{lr}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>lr</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{lr}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, cosine decay to <math id="S7.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="S7.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We compare two diagnostic methods and five correction strategies:</p>
<ul id="S7.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S7.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method A (ours):</span> gradient attribution on misclassified images <math id="S7.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> layer-group surgical correction with physics momentum.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method B (Karoni et al.):</span> per-parameter friction <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> from iKFAD training <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> rank layers by accumulated friction <math id="S7.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> layer-group surgical correction.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Methods C, D:</span> per-parameter correction using top 30% and 15% highest-<math id="S7.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> parameters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S7.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S7.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method E:</span> cross-optimizer transfer—diagnose the Adam model with our gradient attribution, then correct with physics momentum.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S7.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">All corrections retrain for 30 epochs with <math id="S7.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Results: Training Accuracy</h3>

<figure id="S7.T15" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 15: </span>Phase 1 accuracy: five training methods on ResNet-18/CIFAR-10 (200 epochs, seed 42).</figcaption>
<table id="S7.T15.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S7.T15.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T15.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T15.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></th>
<th id="S7.T15.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T15.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Best Test Accuracy</span></th>
<th id="S7.T15.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T15.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Errors</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.T15.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T15.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">CD—Cubic Damping (Karoni et al.)</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S7.T15.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">95.62%</span></td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">453</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T15.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T15.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Baseline (<math id="S7.T15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">95.51%</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">453</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T15.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T15.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">iKFAD (Karoni et al.)</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">95.39%</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">468</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T15.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T15.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Physics (<math id="S7.T15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">95.12%</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center">496</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T15.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T15.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">Adam (<math id="S7.T15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{lr}=10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>lr</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{lr}=10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">93.68%</td>
<td id="S7.T15.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">647</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All four SGD-momentum variants achieve comparable accuracy within a 0.50 pp range (95.12–95.62%). Adam trails by <math id="S7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sim}1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sim}1.8</annotation></semantics></math> pp, consistent with the known generalization gap between SGD and Adam on image classification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.3 </span>Results: Cross-Optimizer Invariance (Key Finding)</h3>

<figure id="S7.T16" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 16: </span>Problem layers identified by each diagnostic method. The SGD–Adam overlap is 100%.</figcaption>
<table id="S7.T16.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S7.T16.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T16.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T16.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem Layers</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt"><span id="S7.T16.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Basis</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T16.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Ours (gradient attr. on SGD baseline)</td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S7.T16.2.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3, conv1, layer2</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Grad norm on errors</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T16.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">iKFAD (per-parameter friction <math id="S7.T16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>)</td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S7.T16.2.3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1, layer3, layer2</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Accumulated friction</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T16.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Ours (gradient attr. on Adam)</td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S7.T16.2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1, layer2, layer3</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left">Grad norm on errors</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T16.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">SGD–iKFAD overlap</td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="S7.T16.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3, layer2</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">2/3 shared</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T16.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S7.T16.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S7.T16.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SGD–Adam overlap</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S7.T16.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">conv1, layer2, layer3</span></td>
<td id="S7.T16.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="S7.T16.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3/3 shared (100%)</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S7.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">This is the central finding of the diagnostic track.</span> Gradient attribution on misclassified images identifies <em id="S7.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exactly the same three problem layers</em> on the SGD baseline and the Adam model—100% overlap. This is not obvious <em id="S7.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">a priori</em>: SGD and Adam traverse fundamentally different optimization trajectories, use different update rules, and produce models with different error counts (453 vs. 647). Yet the architectural bottlenecks that cause errors are the same.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The implication is that gradient attribution on misclassified images measures a property of the <em id="S7.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">architecture</em>—specifically, which layers have insufficient capacity or receive insufficient gradient signal for the hardest examples—rather than an artifact of the optimizer. The diagnostic pipeline is therefore <span id="S7.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">optimizer-agnostic</span>, which is essential for applicability to large models trained with Adam variants.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note the difference from iKFAD: our gradient attribution identifies <span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span> (first convolutional layer, learnable feature detectors), while iKFAD identifies <span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1</span> (batch normalization, only scale/shift parameters). Since <span id="S7.SS3.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span> contains the features responsible for texture–shape confusions, the gradient-attribution diagnosis is more causally meaningful.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.4 </span>Results: Surgical Correction Comparison</h3>

