<tr id="S7.T17.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T17.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Diagnostic</th>
<th id="S7.T17.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">—</th>
<td id="S7.T17.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Grad attr.</td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Friction <math id="S7.T17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Friction <math id="S7.T17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Friction <math id="S7.T17.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Grad attr.</td></tr>
<tr id="S7.T17.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S7.T17.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Granularity</th>
<th id="S7.T17.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">—</th>
<td id="S7.T17.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Layer</td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Layer</td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Param</td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.8.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Param</td>
<td id="S7.T17.2.8.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">Layer</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S7.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Three findings emerge:</p>
</div>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Layer-level correction outperforms parameter-level.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Methods A and B (layer-level) both fix 62 errors, while Methods C and D (parameter-level, top 30% and 15% by friction <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>) fix only 42 and 46 respectively. Moreover, parameter-level methods introduce <em id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">more</em> new errors than they fix, yielding negative net improvement (<math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>17 and <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>10). Simpler granularity wins: at the ResNet-18 scale, layer-group correction constrains the optimization sufficiently to avoid destabilizing adjacent features.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">iKFAD layers produce fewer side effects.</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Methods A and B fix the same number of errors (62), but iKFAD-guided layer selection (Method B) introduces only 40 new errors versus 55 for Method A, achieving net +22 versus +7. The likely explanation: iKFAD identifies <span id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1</span> instead of <span id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">conv1</span>, and correcting batch normalization parameters is lower-risk than modifying the first convolutional layer.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adam cross-optimizer correction (Method E).</h4>

<div id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The diagnostic transfers perfectly (100% layer overlap). Correction fixes 146 errors—the largest number of any method—but also introduces 148 new errors (net <math id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math>2). The Adam-trained weights occupy a different region of parameter space; the correction hyperparameters need optimizer-specific tuning. This is a <em id="S7.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">proof of concept</em>: the diagnostic generalizes; the correction requires adaptation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S8" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Experiment 3b: The Exhaustive Layer-Selection Baseline</h2>

<div id="S8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiments 2–3 reported that surgical correction of diagnostically selected layer groups improves the model: gradient attribution scored net <math id="S8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6</annotation></semantics></math> on the Experiment-2 checkpoint and <math id="S8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+7</annotation></semantics></math> on the Experiment-3 checkpoint (two independently trained baselines with 452 and 453 test errors respectively), and the best variant — iKFAD-guided selection of <span id="S8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1+layer2+layer3</span>, Method B — reported <math id="S8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+22" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>22</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+22</annotation></semantics></math>. In the exhaustive re-run below, that same combination under the standardized correction protocol scores <math id="S8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+9</annotation></semantics></math>, a first hint that individual deltas of this magnitude are dominated by run-to-run variation. Version 2 of this paper presented this as evidence that the diagnostic <em id="S8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">selects which layers to repair</em>. The natural objection—“would any three layers do?”—turns out to be answerable exactly: with 7 layer groups there are only <math id="S8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{7}{3}=35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{7}{3}=35</annotation></semantics></math> possible selections. We ran the identical correction protocol (30 epochs, physics momentum, same checkpoint) on <span id="S8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">all of them</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S8.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span>Exhaustive layer-selection landscape: all 35 combinations of 3-of-7 layer groups, identical surgical protocol on the same baseline checkpoint (453 initial errors). Selected rows; full table in the appendix and released data.</figcaption>
<table id="S8.T18.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S8.T18.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S8.T18.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S8.T18.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank</span></th>
<th id="S8.T18.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S8.T18.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Combination</span></th>
<th id="S8.T18.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S8.T18.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Net errors fixed</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S8.T18.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">conv1 + bn1 + layer3</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S8.T18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+18</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">2</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bn1 + layer3 + layer4</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.T18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+15</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">conv1 + bn1 + layer2</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.T18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+14</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="S8.T18.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S8.T18.2.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">conv1 + layer2 + layer3 (diagnostic pick)</span></td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.T18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{+7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">+</mo><mn>𝟕</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{+7}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">33</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bn1 + layer1 + layer4</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.T18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-13</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">34</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">bn1 + layer4 + fc</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center"><math id="S8.T18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-14" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-14</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S8.T18.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S8.T18.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">35</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">layer1 + layer4 + fc</td>
<td id="S8.T18.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S8.T18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-20</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S8.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The selection claim fails.</span> The diagnostic triple ranks 11th of 35 (exact <math id="S8.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=11/35=0.31" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>35</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.31</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=11/35=0.31</annotation></semantics></math>)—not better than random selection. We note the absolute scale honestly: the entire 35-combination landscape spans roughly <math id="S8.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 0.2</annotation></semantics></math> pp of test accuracy (<math id="S8.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+18" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+18</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S8.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-20</annotation></semantics></math> net errors out of 453 on the 10k test set); its value is methodological—it is the exact null distribution that layer-selection claims should be tested against—rather than practical. Replicates of the diagnostic arm vary by <math id="S8.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> net error (<math id="S8.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6</annotation></semantics></math> on the Experiment-2 checkpoint; <math id="S8.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+7</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S8.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+8</annotation></semantics></math> in two replicates on this section’s checkpoint), consistent with the nondeterminism noted in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiment 1: Multi-Seed Validation of the Schedule ‣ Critical Damping as a Momentum Schedule:Multi-Seed Validation, a Hybrid Recipe, and an ExhaustiveNegative Result on Surgical Layer Selection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The result is not measurement noise: an independent re-run of the diagnostic arm reproduced its net improvement (<math id="S8.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+7</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="S8.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+8</annotation></semantics></math>), so the protocol is stable; the claim is what fails.</p>
</div>
<div id="S8.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">What survives.</span> Two weaker properties of the gradient-norm ranking are real:</p>
<ol id="S8.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S8.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">A soft top-layer signal.</em> The 15 combinations containing <span id="S8.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer3</span>—the top-ranked layer—average <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+6.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>6.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+6.2</annotation></semantics></math> net errors fixed, versus <math id="S8.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1.4</annotation></semantics></math> for the 20 combinations without it.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S8.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S8.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">A reliable harm-avoidance signal.</em> The bottom of the landscape is populated by combinations of the <em id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">lowest</em>-ranked layers (<span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer4</span>, <span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">fc</span>, <span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1</span>-with-<span id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">layer4</span>): the anti-diagnostic pick loses <math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>13</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">13</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="S8.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> net errors. The ranking correctly predicts what <em id="S8.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> to touch.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S8.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S8.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S8.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation.</span> Gradient attribution on misclassified images measures where error-relevant computation concentrates, and its extremes are informative: the highest-norm layer is a good (not optimal) repair target, and low-norm layers are actively dangerous to retrain. But the fine ordering in the middle carries little information about repair outcomes, and combinations were never measured by the diagnostic at all—<span id="S8.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bn1</span>, ranked 6th of 7, appears in all three top combinations. We conclude that layer-selection claims in surgical fine-tuning need combinatorial baselines, and we release the full landscape to make that comparison free for future work at this scale.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">9 </span>Experiment 4: Hybrid Momentum Scheduling</h2>

<div id="S9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Experiment 1 revealed a tension: physics momentum (<math id="S9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=1-2\sqrt{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>) converges to 90% accuracy about twice as fast as baseline (<math id="S9.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.34\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.34</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.34\times</annotation></semantics></math> multi-seed), but baseline (<math id="S9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>) reaches the final 95% sooner (epoch 174 vs. 190 on seed 42). The physics schedule is near-critically damped, which suppresses the oscillation that helps escape shallow local minima in the late-training landscape. Baseline’s underdamped regime acts as implicit exploration, beneficial when the remaining errors involve subtle feature distinctions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This motivates a <span id="S9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">hybrid schedule</span>: use physics momentum for fast early convergence, then switch to baseline momentum for the final push.</p>
</div>
<section id="S9.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<div id="S9.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare five methods on the same setup (ResNet-18, CIFAR-10, 200 epochs, cosine LR, batch 128, seed 42):</p>
<ol id="S9.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S9.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baseline</span>: constant <math id="S9.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Physics</span>: <math id="S9.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(t)=\text{clamp}(1-2\sqrt{\alpha(t)},\;0.5,\;0.99)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>clamp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 0.99</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(t)=\text{clamp}(1-2\sqrt{\alpha(t)},\;0.5,\;0.99)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1cycle</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>: <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> linear <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95{\to}0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.95</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95{\to}0.85</annotation></semantics></math> over the first half of training, back to <math id="S9.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math> over the second.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid-90</span>: physics momentum until test accuracy <math id="S9.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 90\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 90\%</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S9.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S9.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S9.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid-ep52</span>: physics momentum until epoch 52 (fixed), then <math id="S9.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S9.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S9.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The two hybrid variants test adaptive (accuracy-triggered) versus fixed (epoch-triggered) switching. The fixed switch point (epoch 52) was chosen, at design time, from the physics 90% crossing observed in the run that preceded this experiment; on the committed Experiment-1 seed-42 data that crossing is epoch 51.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S9.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">9.2 </span>Results</h3>

